**If this fails**, you've found the problem. The most likely failure modes at an edge store location:

| Error you'll see | Root cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `no such host: registry-1.docker.io` | DNS can't resolve Docker Hub | Fix DNS, or point to internal registry |
| `connection timed out` | Firewall/proxy blocks outbound 443 to Docker Hub | Open egress, or use proxy |
| `x509: certificate signed by unknown authority` | TLS interception proxy (Zscaler/Palo Alto) not trusted | Add corporate CA to OS trust |
| `manifest unknown` / `404` | Version tag truly doesn't exist | Change cluster K8s version |
| `toomanyrequests` / `401 unauthorized` | Docker Hub rate limit | Auth or internal mirror |
| Pull hangs/is slow | MTU or proxy issue | Investigate network |

